== living | EVENING · FAMILY HOME | warm African family living room at evening with a big sofa, family photos and a TV | sofa
kemi (worried): Quddus, tonight I'm telling my parents I want to study abroad. My mum will cry. My dad will ask who will fix the generator.
quddus (talk): Their worry comes from love. So don't just announce it. Bring a plan.
kemi (think): A plan?
quddus (talk): Which program, how it's funded, where you'll live, and how you'll stay in touch. Facts calm fears.
> 1f4cb | YOUR FAMILY PLAN | 1f393 The program + why it matters | 1f4b0 How it's paid for | 1f3e0 Where you'll live | 1f4f1 How you'll keep in touch

== park | NEXT MORNING · FAMILY GARDEN | sunny family garden with a mango tree, flowers and plastic chairs | bench
kemi (cheer): Quddus, it worked! Mum cried, but happy tears. Dad asked for the university website.
quddus (thumbs): That's beautiful. What changed their mind?
kemi (talk): I showed them the scholarship letter, the accommodation, and that I'd call every Sunday.
quddus (talk): And you listened to their worries too. That's what makes it a family decision.
kemi (cheer): And I taught my little brother how to fix the generator. Family plan complete!
